<title>UK: London tea auction report.</title>
<headline>London tea auction report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The London tea auction of 9,545 packages saw strong general demand on Monday, the official report said.</p>
<p>In the landed sector, prices for Quality Assams ranged between 150 pence and 208 pence per kg, with coloury good liquoring types making 130-145 pence per kg.</p>
<p>Bright, useful Kenyas and Burundis improved to 120-136 pence per kg with best Burundi PD's seeing 190-200 pence per kg.</p>
<p>Mediums were generally up 3-5 pence.</p>
<p>Offshores saw good demand at firm rates.</p>
<p>-Londn Newsroom, +44 171 542 8071</p>
</text>
